body='<section class="note">The sequence describes the actual application, including its optional shared-file branch. Fallback activation is conditional and is not claimed by a normal healthy run. Each numbered step below includes a source-labelled excerpt.</section><a class="button" href="/architecture.svg" download>Download UML SVG</a><div class="diagram"><img src="/architecture.svg" alt="Thirteen steps for selecting models and verifying environment and directories"></div>'
for s in steps:
 n=s['number'];body+=f'<section class="step workflow-step" id="workflow-step-{n:02}"><span class="number">{n:02}</span><h3>{n}. {escape(s["title"])}</h3><p>{escape(s["explanation"])}</p><p class="source">Source: {s["source"]} · lines {s["firstLine"]}–{s["lastLine"]}</p><p class="meta">Selected source; surrounding implementation is omitted and display whitespace is reformatted.</p>'+snippet(s['code'])+f'<h4>How this code explains step {n}</h4><p>{escape(s["explanation"])}</p></section>'
document('/architecture.html','Architecture and <em>UML workflow.</em>','Follow every step from validated options to actual subprocess evidence and formatted results.',body+actions(('/','← Application'),('/walkthrough.html','Code walkthrough →')))
reference=[('model','Alias or full ID; this lab pins three IDs. Aliases such as haiku, sonnet and opus move over time. Newer deck examples are not promises of account access.'),('fallbackModel','A distinct backup, or a supported comma-separated chain. The app exposes one backup. Overload handling and primary retry are documented behavior, not induced here.'),('effort','The SDK type supports low, medium, high, xhigh and max. Model support varies. This UI limits Sonnet/Opus to low, medium and high; pinned Haiku omits effort.'),('thinking','adaptive, enabled with budgetTokens, or disabled. This app uses adaptive with display omitted or disabled. Summarized display is a supported public summary where available, never raw private reasoning.'),('env','TypeScript replaces the subprocess environment; spread process.env. Python merges explicit values over inheritance. This app executes only TypeScript.'),('cwd / additionalDirectories','cwd picks the project for a new session. Additional directories add file access, not their settings. This lab sets settingSources to [] and does not demonstrate configuration discovery.'),('Not a latency guarantee','Effort and model choices can affect cost and response behavior, but provider load, caching and task variation matter. These small observations do not establish a universal ranking.')]
body=cards(reference)+''.join(f'<section class="step"><h3>{s["number"]}. {escape(s["title"])}</h3><p>{escape(s["explanation"])}</p><p class="source">{s["source"]} · line {s["firstLine"]}</p>'+snippet(s['code'])+'</section>' for s in steps)
body+='<section class="note"><h3>Python mapping · reference only</h3>'+snippet('ClaudeAgentOptions(\n    model="claude-sonnet-4-6",\n    fallback_model="claude-opus-4-6",\n    cwd="/classroom/alpha",\n    add_dirs=["/classroom/shared"],\n    env={"LESSON10_CONTEXT": "lesson10-alpha"},\n)','python')+'<p>This is a spelling reference. No Python SDK process is started by this app. Do not assume identical environment merge behavior.</p></section>'
body+='<p>References: <a href="https://code.claude.com/docs/en/agent-sdk/configuration">SDK configuration</a> · <a href="https://code.claude.com/docs/en/model-config">Model configuration</a> · <a href="https://code.claude.com/docs/en/agent-sdk/typescript">TypeScript reference</a></p>'
document('/walkthrough.html','How the app <em>was built.</em>','Read the real implementation and distinguish executed experiments from the broader lesson reference.',body)
readme='# Claude Agent SDK · Lesson 10 · Models, effort and environment\n\nBased on Lesson10_Models_Effort_and_Environment.pptx. A TypeScript classroom lab with five linked student pages, large text, source-linked UML steps and actual SDK evidence.\n\n## What you will learn\n\n'+''.join(f'- {a}: {b}\n' for a,b in learn)
readme+='\n## Configure and run\n\nUse Node.js 24+, npm and your own Anthropic API key with access to the chosen model. Python is not needed to run the app.\n\n```powershell\ngit clone https://github.com/luiscoco/Udemy-Claude-Agent-SDK-lesson10-app.git\ncd .\\Udemy-Claude-Agent-SDK-lesson10-app\nnpm ci\nif (!(Test-Path .env)) { Copy-Item .env.example .env }\nnotepad .env\nnpm start\n```\n\nFrom presentations use `cd .\\agent-sdk\\lesson10-models-environment` instead of cloning. Open http://127.0.0.1:3110. Keep the terminal open; Ctrl+C stops it.\n\n## Create your .env file\n\nPreserve an existing .env; otherwise copy .env.example. Enter your key locally and restart after changing it. The start and sample:env scripts explicitly load the optional file. Shell variables take precedence. Never commit the real file.\n\n```dotenv\n'+env+'\n```\n\nOn Windows, if needed, set `CLAUDE_CODE_GIT_BASH_PATH=C:/Program Files/Git/bin/bash.exe` after verifying your actual installation. Keep optional dependencies enabled. An existing instance prints its URL; choose another PORT for an unrelated listener.\n\n## Run the experiments\n\n'
for i,(t,d,c) in enumerate(runsteps[2:7],1):readme+=f'{i}. {t}: {d}\n'
readme+='\n```powershell\nnpm run sample:env -- 1\nnpm run sample:env -- 0\nnpm run sample:env -- 2\nnpm test\n```\n\n`sample` uses only the launching shell environment. Run browser and terminal samples sequentially. Model access and provider errors remain actual outcomes. No fixture answer replaces a failed request.\n\n## How the app was built\n\n'
for s in steps:readme+=f'### {s["number"]}. {s["title"]}\n\n{s["explanation"]}\n\nSource: `{s["source"]}`, line {s["firstLine"]}. Selected source; surrounding code omitted.\n\n```typescript\n{s["code"]}\n```\n\n'
readme+='## Boundaries and reference material\n\n'+''.join(f'- {a}: {b}\n' for a,b in reference)+'\nThe application exposes only trusted fixture paths and one exact context command. These application checks are not an OS sandbox. Model answers render with the bundled Markdown parser and sanitizer. Thinking text is not exposed. Cost is an SDK estimate with a threshold, not a precise invoice guarantee.\n\n## References\n\n- [Agent SDK configuration](https://code.claude.com/docs/en/agent-sdk/configuration)\n- [Model configuration](https://code.claude.com/docs/en/model-config)\n- [TypeScript reference](https://code.claude.com/docs/en/agent-sdk/typescript)\n\nOptional documentation regeneration: `python scripts/build-pages.py`. Source excerpts are validated against real source anchors.\n'
(APP/'README.md').write_text(readme,encoding='utf-8')
print('Built five Lesson 10 student pages and 13 source-linked UML steps.')
